d_category_count":1},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"SYCGlb0WFyyVxD2K9Z-YuA","review_id":"SOMfoXX8H_RozhhOGunwiQ","date":"2018-06-14T17:01:25","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9461277723312378,"text_excerpt":"I went for lunch last week with a group of work peeps. Only 1 of us opted for the lunch buffet which was very meaty, if that's your thing. The rest of us ordered off the menu: 1 shrimp poboy, 2 ital plates, 1 jerk chicken and 1 mixed jerk plate. I loved my ital plate... callaloo, beans & rice, plantains and a veg...OK the veg that day was cooked cabbage which is not my favorite but it was a good value for the money and I actually ate the rest at a 2nd meal. My coworkers enjoyed their poboy and jerk chicken. The person who had the buffet loved the variety of meats (which are unlabeled so ask if there is something you don't/can't eat). The service was really friendly and the decor was basic..."},{"business_id":"SYCGlb0WFyyVxD2K9Z-YuA","review_id":"FNrzkI3wuB0VQc9UhkIVmg","date":"2011-09-12T20:31:00","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.942261815071106,"text_excerpt":"I can't believe I haven't reviewed this place, as I've been raving about it for at least a year now. Boswells is one of the first places I want to go whenever we are away from New Orleans for awhile. The Jamaican Jerk Chicken and Pork lunches are fantastic, and dont' forget to grab some coco bread (tastes much better than what it looks like which is rolls from KFC) and their meat and vegetable meat pies, which taste wonderful up to a week later. I can't wait to eat there next, and the people there have always been very polite and attentive."},{"business_id":"SYCGlb0WFyyVxD2K9Z-YuA","review_id":"2dPIzrGZPJkNSk79yKfptg","date":"2017-02-13T22:00:01","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9420684576034546,"text_excerpt":"I went on a lunch date. We had the buffet. I enjoyed the rice & peas and the stewed chicken. It was pretty good. The star of meal was the Mac and cheese. I was shocked. It was the best I ever had at a Jamaican spot. I've visited Boswell's before this date and I waited at the counter for 10 minutes and no one took my order. I thought I was invisible. I vowed to never return but my date insisted. I'm glad he did. I will return. I have missed the abundance of Caribbean food where I'm from and it feels good to know that there is somewhere to go in Nola to get my fix. *I will update this review as I try more of the menu."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"SYCGlb0WFyyVxD2K9Z-YuA","photo_id":"BR44PWTfRqOjDM5PTMaFCw","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/BR44PWTfRqOjDM5PTMaFCw.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.9556041955947876},{"business_id":"SYCGlb0WFyyVxD2K9Z-YuA","photo_id":"IOtAogpuwStfLXfTFt3Xdg","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/IOtAogpuwStfLXfTFt3Xdg.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.9376068711280823},{"business_id":"SYCGlb0WFyyVxD2K9Z-YuA","photo_id":"cVcr3Vxhtnmdc3F2_9N6Ng","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/cVcr3Vxhtnmdc3F2_9N6Ng.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.9317752122879028},{"business_id":"SYCGlb0WFyyVxD2K9Z-YuA","photo_id":"wOmK15BDXssnX9hjoy-ZvQ","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/wOmK15BDXssnX9hjoy-ZvQ.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.9088106155395508}]},"notebook_case":null}
